Writing One Line at a Time 

In some cases, multiple characters may need to be written to a file. For              
instance, an entire line of characters is to be written to a text file. This operation can                 
be performed by using function ​fputs()​, at which its function prototype is given as              
follows. 

int fputs(const char *s, FILE *stream); 

Function ​fputs() writes an array of character pointed by​char ​pointer ​s to the              
file stream. It returns a non-negative integer upon successful operation. Otherwise, it            
returns ​EOF ​on error. An example of how to usefputs() to write a block of characters                 
to a file is given in Listing 11-4. 

/* File:  block2file.c  */ 
#include <stdio.h> 
#include <stdlib.h> 
int main()  
