Reading a Block of Data 

In order to read a block of data from a file, C programming provides a               
function ​fread()​ to perform this operation. The function prototype is given below. 

size_t fread(void *ptr, size_t size, size_t nelem, FILE *stream); 

Function ​fread() ​also receives four arguments similar to its counterpart,          
fwrite()​. If it returns a value less than​nelem​, either​EOF ​or read error is encountered.                
Listing 11-6 illustrates an example of using function​fread() for reading structure data             
from a binary file.  
/* File:  file2record.c  */ 
